<br>
Alas, the next day it was<br>
their turn to give in...</i><br>
We were shown the way<br>
As far back as Quiberon.<br>
<br>
<i>Five or six days later<br>
there, on Quiberon's beach<br>
The cannonballs were raining<br>
thick as a swarm of bees.</i><br>
<br>
3. Then George and La-Vendée<br>
<i>Then George and La-Vendée<br>
They asked for the head<br>
the head of the army.</i><br>
<br>
The head of the army they took<br>
<i>as soon as they found it.<br>
To lead the battle on the shore<br>
they were hired instantly.</i><br>
<br>
But no good news anymore<br>
Was to reach them that day.<br>
<i>There was obviously</i><br>
Betrayal on the way.<br>
<br>
Georges ordered us:<br>
Quickly retreat! Quickly!<br>
<i>He gathered all his men<br>
to take them all on board<br>
<br>
Eight or nine vessels:</i><br>
